The Roundhat Gang is a protection racket in [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/index|Sableclutch]]. Its run by [[Tywelwyn Leatherhide]] out of [[The Crowded Flea]]. Recently, it appears to have established some kind of partnership with [[Org/Pyrelight/index|Pyrelight]].

Under [[Tywelwyn Leatherhide]], the Roundhat Gang operates with whatever authority its leader's reputation can command.

Its members gather at [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/The Crowded Flea|The Crowded Flea]], where their bouncer's round hat marks the tavern as theirs. A tall half-giant, [[Org/Roundhat Gang/People/Hlarf|Hlarf]], holds court among them there, the one who speaks for the gang to outsiders. When Johnny came asking after [[Org/Roundhat Gang/People/Tywelwyn Leatherhide|Tywelwyn]], the half-giant said that if Tywelwyn found Johnny interesting he might meet him the next evening at six on [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/Pier 54|Pier 54]]. Its protection racket reaches businesses across Sableclutch, including the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/Second Sun Diner|Second Sun Diner]], whose rooftop dish the gang installed. As the endless rain flooded the district, Tywelwyn told his people to pack up and move; one of his henchmen knew of the order but not where or why they were going. The convox has posted five hundred gold pieces for Tywelwyn, brought in or killed.

Every member the Party could pick out on a stakeout had something of an animal about him on top of human stock, and the gang are [[Bestiary/Werecreature|werecreatures]]: the ones in the tavern turned into boars, rats and a crocodile. [[Org/Roundhat Gang/People/Hlarf|Hlarf]] speaks for them. One night in the endless rain the Party appeared by magic in the tavern's back room to take the gang by surprise. [[Tywelwyn Leatherhide|Tywelwyn]] was not there, and the gang killed three of the Party in the room; the fourth escaped out the window. The Party killed a rat and a boar of the gang before they were brought down.
